# Pin source + proof files to LF regardless of core.autocrlf / platform.
# HB-0065: several scribe proofs anchor a literal char immediately before `\n`
# in a cross-line regex over checked-out source; on a CRLF checkout (Windows —
# the field machines' platform) those `\n`-anchored matches false-fail and red the
# green-gate even though the product code is correct. Forcing LF here makes the
# proofs deterministic across platforms (the product never depends on EOL).
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
NOTICE text eol=lf
integrations/vscode/LICENSE.txt text eol=lf
# The Godot addon under assets/vulcan/addon/ is embedded byte-for-byte into a
# generated module, and the vulcan suite's first step compares the checked-out
# bytes with the committed module: a CRLF checkout turned every .gd and .cfg
# file into drift and reddened the suite before a prover ran, and the
# discovery prover's cross-line anchor over plugin.gd failed the same way.
# Pinned to LF on every platform, with the Python drivers (read by the same
# class of cross-line checks) beside them.
*.gd   text eol=lf
*.cfg  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
scripts/vendor/patches/*.patch text eol=lf
